{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaKeystoneInteraction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaKeystoneInteraction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:c_3_keystone_structure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"c_3_keystone_structure","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaKeystoneInteraction.lean#L60-L68","doc":"Theorem: The c_3 keystone structurally factors into the exact Higgs/Trefoil interaction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:c_3_keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"c_3_keystone","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaKeystoneInteraction.lean#L53-L58","doc":"The proposed Q_beta c_3 keystone from the T_{3,5} and 4_1 knot interaction.\n-Vol(4_1) represents the Higgs 4_1 baseline.\n`u` is the linear substrate deformation.\n`- interaction_factor * u^2` is the back-reaction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:interaction_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"interaction_factor","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaKeystoneInteraction.lean#L50-L51","doc":"The Q_beta interaction factor driven by the T_{3,5} back-reaction on the electron trefoil. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:crossings_T_3_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"crossings_T_3_5","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaKeystoneInteraction.lean#L47-L48","doc":"The topological crossing number of the beta-decay torus knot (T_{3,5}). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:crossings_3_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"crossings_3_1","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaKeystoneInteraction.lean#L44-L45","doc":"The topological crossing number of the electron trefoil (3_1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:substrate_u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"substrate_u","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaKeystoneInteraction.lean#L41-L42","doc":"The topological substrate deformation parameter `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Vol_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Vol_4_1","kind":"def","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaKeystoneInteraction.lean#L15-L39","doc":"A 16-significant-digit DECIMAL TRUNCATION of the figure-eight volume.\n\nThe docstring here read \"The exact continuum volume of the figure-eight knot\n4_1. Defined via the Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm.\" Both clauses were false, and\nin the direction that matters: this is a hardcoded literal, and nothing in\nthis file evaluates a dilogarithm. Measured against the corpus's exact\ncarrier `QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1 = 2 * Cl_2 (π/3)`:\n\n    this def   2.029883212819307\n    exact      2.0298832128193072500424051085490…\n    difference 2.500424051085490e-16   (1.232e-16 relative)\n\nSo `Vol_4_1 ≠ QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1` — the same defect bean\n`qou-f8lit` records for `Encounter/MostowRigidity.figureEight`, which was\nrepaired by pointing at the exact carrier instead.\n\nIt is NOT repaired the same way here, deliberately. This declaration has\n**zero consumers**: `c_3_keystone_structure` takes `V_4_1` as a parameter and\nnever reads it, and the one module importing this file\n(`QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalAction`) does not reference it either. Making\nit exact would add a dependency to a file whose CORRECTIVE NOTE above states\nits whole content is hardcoded literals with no mathematical content, and\nwould move no number anywhere. Use `QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1` if\nyou need the volume; do not cite this. ","signatureChunk":0}]}